# .clinerules — noor (نور)
# Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem — watermark: ALLAH
#
# These rules are binding for any AI assistant or contributor generating
# or modifying code in this repository. They are not suggestions.

## 1. Offline-First, Always
- ZERO ad SDKs. ZERO third-party analytics. ZERO remote telemetry.
- ZERO network calls of any kind (no HTTP clients, no sockets, no
  remote config, no crash reporters that phone home).
- All data — Quran text, azkar, prayer calculation constants, user
  settings — ships in the app bundle or lives in the local encrypted
  SQLite database. If a feature seems to need the internet, stop and
  redesign it to work offline.

## 2. File Size Discipline
- No single `.dart` file may exceed 150 lines of code.
- If a widget, cubit, or repository grows past that limit, split it:
  extract sub-widgets, split state classes, or break repositories into
  smaller focused classes.

## 3. Decoupled Layers (strict one-way dependency)
- `presentation/` (widgets/screens) MUST NOT import `sqflite_sqlcipher`,
  write raw SQL, or perform prayer-time/date math directly.
- `presentation/` talks only to `logic/` (Cubit/Bloc).
- `logic/` talks only to `data/` (repositories) for persistence and to
  `core/` services (haptics, location, database) for hardware/IO.
- `data/` owns all SQL and all direct package calls (adhan, sqflite,
  geolocator). It exposes plain Dart models, never raw DB rows, to
  `logic/`.

## 4. Accessibility Is Not Optional
- Every interactive widget (buttons, list tiles, switches, sliders,
  counters) MUST be wrapped in an explicit `Semantics()` widget with a
  meaningful `label` and, where relevant, `hint` and `value`.
- Screen-reader users (VoiceOver/TalkBack) must be able to operate 100%
  of app functionality without sighted assistance.

## 5. SQL & Performance
- All SQL queries MUST be parameterized (`?` placeholders) — never
  string-interpolate user or dynamic values into SQL.
- Favor indexed lookups and small result sets; this app targets
  low-RAM/low-end hardware.

## 6. Haptics (Tasbih)
- `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` fires on every tap.
- A distinct heavier/double pulse fires on milestone counts: 33, 66, 100.

## 7. Watermark
- Major source files (entry points, core services, cubits, primary
  screens) carry a short header comment containing the watermark
  "ALLAH". This is a project convention, not a license notice.
